🔥 Common Interview Traps

❌ Assuming input() returns an integer.

✔ input() always returns a string.

❌ Forgetting to convert input before performing arithmetic.

age = input("Age: ")

age + 5 ❌

Correct

age = int(input("Age: "))

❌ Confusing indexing with slicing.

name[2]

returns one character.

name[2:5]

returns a substring.

❌ Forgetting to use strip() before comparing user input.

" yes "

is not equal to

"yes"

unless strip() is used.

❌ Case-sensitive comparisons.

Always use

user_input.strip().lower()

before comparing text entered by users.

